WEBVTT

NOTE Visual text from a silent video.

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.400
“Ana” can refer to more than one contact.

2
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:14.100
Validation must require an unambiguous identity, not a guess.

3
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:22.000
Resolving the argument does not replace approval to send.

4
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:29.400
The query expected three records but received only two.

5
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:36.100
The tool returns the available data and marks the result as partial.

6
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:44.000
The runtime keeps track of what is missing so it can recover or stop.

7
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:52.100
Context is the working view the model receives for this turn.

8
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:59.500
Memory retains information; the runtime keeps operations and events.

9
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:08.000
Only relevant information is projected into the decision context.

10
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:15.400
The window must hold instructions, tools, history and working data.

11
00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:22.100
It also needs an output reserve and safety headroom.

12
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:30.000
When retrieval grows too large, select context rather than erasing those reserves.

13
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:37.400
An operation can be accepted and still be running.

14
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:44.100
After a failure, it may retry before ending in an error.

15
00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:52.000
That path does not justify reporting successful completion.

16
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:59.400
A stored fact can become stale or conflict with another source.

17
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:06.100
Keep its provenance and check evidence before using it.

18
00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:14.000
Memory needs rules for correction, expiration and deletion.
